    "done_when": "Stop the candidates snapshot walking the whole docs tree on every pick. The snapshot-stall investigation (~/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/snapshot-stall-under-load/report.md and timings.json) measured routing._estimated_hours (reckon/crew/routing.py line 3641, called from reckon/crew/picker/snapshot.py) at 93-95% of the snapshot: 993 ms median idle and 1,362 ms under load, at most 1,596 ms. When a node carries no estimated hours, it runs docs.rglob(\"*.html\") over the whole docs tree on GPFS to find the node's plan, uncached, on every pick.\n\n1. Resolve the node's plan without walking the tree. Find the plan by its slug through the resolver reckon.resources already uses to locate one plan, or cache the slug-to-path index on the stamps of the directories it read, the way routing.context_census caches on file stamps. The returned hours and source must be identical for every node the current code handles: node-supplied hours, a plan found, a plan not found, and an empty plan name.\n2. Tests in tests/test_estimated_hours_reads_one_plan.py:\n   - Equality: for a synthetic docs tree with several plans, nested directories and evidence fragments, the new _estimated_hours returns the same (hours, source) as the walk for every node. Compute the expected value in the test from the same fixture.\n   - Walk count: a second call for the same plan performs no directory walk, counted with an instrumented rglob or os.scandir.\n   - Stamp: editing the plan file changes the returned hours on the next call.\n3. Measure _estimated_hours on the live reckon docs tree before and after, five calls each, median and maximum, and record both in the manifest. The after-median must be under 50 ms.\n4. Negative control: restoring the per-call rglob walk makes the walk-count test fail.\n\nDo not edit reckon/crew/dispatch.py or reckon/cli.py; they are on hold for a module split. Gate: tests/test_estimated_hours_reads_one_plan.py, tests/test_pick_candidates_one_pass.py, every tests/test_picker*.py, and every tests/ file that imports reckon.crew.routing. Build that list from your head tree with grep -l. Run with the main checkout's .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 in the FOREGROUND, with one log each for base and head under the run directory, each ending in an EXIT line, judged by delta. Write the evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/one-typesafe-model-picker/estimated-hours-reads-one-plan.html.",
